edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508710 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508710 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cb2e1c85-661c-5c30-a579-2a791c364ae9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508890 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508890 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508532 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508890 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508657 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508890 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508890 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508710 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508890 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508890 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508890 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186508447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508890 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d4fdc251-4753-54c7-b5d7-bf5f38519bcc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508990 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508890 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508990 #edb/ref 1069 "q-106807" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508990 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508990 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $P$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ real matrices $A=({a}_{ij})$ such that ${a}_{22}=0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. For any $A,B\\in P$ and any $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (A+B)=\\alpha A+\\alpha B.$\n\nII. The scalar multiplication of matrices in $P$ is associative.\n\nIII. For any $A\\in P,$ we have $1\\cdot A={I}_{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508990 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e4e1e0d5-3773-5038-a8b4-577c1254dd92" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508990 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's verify the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrices $A=({a}_{ij})$ and $B=({b}_{ij})$ from $P,$ the entries are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha ({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij})=\\alpha {a}_{ij}+\\alpha {b}_{ij},\n$$\n\nand hence,\n\n$$\n\\alpha (A+B)=\\alpha A+\\alpha B.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matric $A=({a}_{ij})$ from $P,$ the entries are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha (\\beta {a}_{ij})=(\\alpha \\beta ){a}_{ij},\n$$\n\nand hence,\n\n$$\n\\alpha (\\beta A)=(\\alpha \\beta )A.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ from $P.$ Then,\n\n$$\n1\\cdot A=1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1\\cdot 1 & 1\\cdot 0 \\\\ 1\\cdot 1 & 1\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\ne {I}_{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186509002 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0c665127-012e-5722-82c0-c620231782dc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186509002 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186281527 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186509016 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186509002 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186509016 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6fe086d3-2ba5-5ffd-ac7b-c7f62891a1d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186509016 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186281526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186509017 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186509016 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186509017 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8061fe35-5bb2-5a7a-a40b-747237b37284" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186509017 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186508990 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186509026 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186509029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186509026 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b1ceacff-cce5-592c-aeca-52a40311b2f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186509026 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186360469 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186509029 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186509017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186509029 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b3319bae-270f-56a4-8501-7d24a9dbec5a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186509029 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124765 #edb/ref 1759218604